{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Ox Named Black: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja29'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 29 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kuruṅgavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Four-horned Antelope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>9. Kaṇhajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Ox Named Black: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yato yato garu dhuraṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>No matter how heavy the load, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yato gambhīravattanī; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>or how deep the passage, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tadāssu kaṇhaṁ yuñjanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when they harness Black, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>svāssu taṁ vahate dhuran”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>he pulls that load. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Kaṇhajātakaṁ navamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
